<h1>Task Groups for Renewals</h1>

<p>
    Task groups are pre-made checklists of tasks that you can apply to renewals. Instead of creating the same tasks over and over for each renewal, you create a task group once and then apply it whenever you need it. This saves time and ensures consistency across your renewals.
</p>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Screenshot showing a task group being applied to a renewal, with a before/after view: renewal with no tasks, then the same renewal after applying a task group showing all the tasks populated. Use visual indicators to show the transformation. -->

<h2>What is a Task Group?</h2>

<p>
    A task group is a template that contains a list of tasks in a specific order. Each task in the group has:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>A name</strong> - What the task is (e.g., "Request Loss Runs", "Create Proposal", "Renew in AMS")</li>
    <li><strong>A description</strong> – Additional details about what needs to be done</li>
    <li><strong>A goal date offset</strong> – How many days before the expiration date this task should be completed</li>
    <li><strong>An assigned person</strong> – Who is typically responsible for this task (optional)</li>
    <li><strong>Subtasks</strong> – Smaller steps that are part of a larger task (optional)</li>
</ul>

<p>
    When you apply a task group to a renewal, Quickfire creates all these tasks automatically, calculates the goal dates based on the renewal's expiration date, and assigns them to the right people.
</p>

<!-- IMAGE PLACEHOLDER: Screenshot of the Task Group Administration page showing a task group with its list of tasks. Show the task names, descriptions, day offsets, and assigned users. Use a visual layout that makes the structure clear. -->

<h2>Why Use Task Groups?</h2>

<p>
    Task groups offer several benefits:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Save time</strong> – Instead of manually creating 10-15 tasks for each renewal, apply a group and they're all created at once</li>
    <li><strong>Ensure consistency</strong> – Every renewal gets the same standard set of tasks, so nothing gets forgotten</li>
    <li><strong>Maintain best practices</strong> – As you refine your process, update the task group and all future renewals will use the improved version</li>
    <li><strong>Organize by line of business</strong> – Create different task groups for different types of policies (General Liability, Workers' Comp, Commercial Auto, etc.)</li>
    <li><strong>Set proper timelines</strong> – Goal dates are calculated automatically based on the expiration date, so tasks are scheduled appropriately</li>
</ul>

