<h2>Creating a Task Group</h2>

<p>
    To create a new task group:
</p>

<ol>
    <li>Go to <strong>Renewals</strong> → <strong>Task Admin</strong> (or navigate to the Master Task Group Administration page)</li>
    <li>Click <strong>New Task Group</strong></li>
    <li>Give your task group a name (e.g., "General Liability Renewal Tasks" or "Workers' Comp Standard Process")</li>
    <li>Add a description if helpful (this is for your reference)</li>
    <li>Start adding tasks to the group:
        <ul>
            <li>You can add existing master tasks (tasks that are already in the system)</li>
            <li>Or create new master tasks as you build the group</li>
            <li>Arrange them in the order they should be completed</li>
            <li>Set the day offset for each task (e.g., "Request Loss Runs" might be 60 days before expiration)</li>
        </ul>
    </li>
    <li>Save the task group</li>
</ol>

<p>
    Once created, the task group is available to apply to any renewal.
</p>

