<h2>Understanding Day Offsets</h2>

<p>
    Day offsets tell the system when each task should be completed relative to the policy expiration date. For example:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>60 days before</strong> – A task with a -60 offset should be done 60 days before the policy expires</li>
    <li><strong>30 days before</strong> – A task with a -30 offset should be done 30 days before expiration</li>
    <li><strong>0 days</strong> – A task with a 0 offset should be done on the expiration date</li>
    <li><strong>No offset</strong> – A task with no offset won't have an automatic goal date</li>
</ul>

<p>
    When you apply a task group to a renewal with an expiration date of, say, December 31st, a task with a -60 day offset will get a goal date of November 1st (60 days before December 31st).
</p>

