<h2>Best Practices</h2>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Start simple</strong> – Create a basic task group first, then refine it as you learn what works</li>
    <li><strong>Test with a few renewals</strong> – Apply a new task group to a few renewals and see how it works before using it everywhere</li>
    <li><strong>Name clearly</strong> – Use descriptive names like "GL Renewal - Standard" so it's obvious which group to use</li>
    <li><strong>Set realistic offsets</strong> – Make sure day offsets give enough time to complete tasks without being too early</li>
    <li><strong>Review regularly</strong> – Periodically review your task groups to see if they need updates</li>
    <li><strong>Document in descriptions</strong> – Use task descriptions to explain why a task is important or how to do it</li>
    <li><strong>Assign default owners</strong> – Set default assignments so tasks go to the right people automatically</li>
</ul>

